I saw an interesting post on our  subreddit at david pakman.com slash  reddit titled is Hillary Clinton  president and I thought it was an  interesting post because at this point  the obsession from the right with  Hillary Clinton is almost as if she were  President of the United States and not  Donald Trump and I know that she did get  millions more votes than Donald Trump in  the 2016 election but the president is  Donald Trump and even the President  himself continues to be obsessed with  Hillary Clinton tweeting about her  endlessly Fox News keeps talking about  Hillary's uranium one scandal a Hillary  investigation when will we finally know  the truth about Hillary this or Hillary  that and there are even a number of  youtubers who I've mentioned before some  of them are sort of making a business  out of criticizing and supposedly  debunking me some of them are also still  talking about if and when or for what  reason is Hillary Clinton going to be  indicted and it's happening to such a  degree and so constantly that if a  foreigner who wasn't following American  politics came to the United States they  check into their hotel they walk through  their hotel lobby and lo and behold that  happens to be Fox News that's on in the  hotel lobby they might actually think  that Hillary Clinton is President of the  United States because of the constant  focus on her by right-wing media rather  than what is actually being done by this  administration and there's a couple  different interpretations here one is  that the Hillary in an orange jumpsuit  conspiracies as I call them they're just  good for ratings and good for business  right the Fox News audience eats it up  and when I say the Fox News audience I  don't literally mean just Fox News I  mean people who primarily get their news  from Fox News or Alex Jones or Rush  Limbaugh whatever whatever you want to  insert there they've been primed for  years to expect Hillary Clinton to be  indicted and put in prison any day now  so it could just be a matter of it's  good for ratings and it does well with  them it titillates an excite  them there's another explanation for the  focus on Hillary Clinton though it's  more cynical and it relates more to the  propaganda motive than the ratings modem  which is that it's a desperate attempt  not to cover and not to inform Trump's  base about the endless scandals and  possible crimes of the Trump  administration and it's all funny and  silly make fun of the stupid right-wing  media and its followers but it has a  real impact because when the focus is on  Hillary Clinton on so much of right-wing  media it reduces the appetite for  holding Trump to account right if people  don't know what's going on with the  actual president the real administration  and instead they're focused on uranium  one Benghazi who knows what her emails  there's going to be no impetus for  actually holding the people from Trump's  administration accountable so I think  it's really easy for us to laugh it off  say look at those stupid brainwashed  people who think what Fox News's agenda  is actually reflects what's happening in  this country but it has a real impact  and we we may see it and I would argue  we're already seeing it and that a lot  of people just aren't worried about what  Trump is doing because they have no clue  what it is that Trump is doing I don't  think we can laugh this off well I think  as far as Fox News is concerned there  has to be a boogeyman right and for the  longest time they had the Democrats they  had Barack Obama they had Hillary  Clinton yep and now Republicans are in  charge of everything Congress the  presidency they got it all so they have  to find something and you know sometimes  they'll focus on the news media but you  can't really single in on any specific  person you're not gonna yes ice Brian  seltzer Brooke Baldwin all over and over  again you gotta go with a Hillary  Clinton although Trump has had some  success in just making the media the  enemy other than of course Fox News was  just doing really really great work  according to him there is always two  layers to these disinformation and  propaganda campaigns and it's very easy  for us on the Left to initially react by  just saying haha how stupid are they but  once we realize right that for every one  of them who has no idea what's going on  we need to make up for that person by  getting someone out to the vote in order  to counter that vote  so the problem we're facing is that it  is a bigger issue than just talking  about the issues it's the entire  narrative that's framed by propaganda  and propagandists who seek to defend  Trump and I've talked about this before  there's actually a couple slides from my  classes that have done at Boston College  and some of my public speaking where I  talk about degrees of informational  incongruity level one of informational  incongruity is we know about an issue we  recognize its importance and we disagree  on the issue so for the example of  abortion we have people who say abortion  should be legal and safe and others who  say abortion is illegal but everybody  agrees abortion is an issue and it is an  important issue level two of  informational incongruity would be a  debate as to the importance of an issue  so on gay marriage as an example you  could have some who say gay marriage is  an important issue and others who say it  is not you need to agree about the  importance of an issue in order to  discuss your positions and the most  dangerous level of informational  incongruity is what I call level 3 and  that is where people are unaware of  something as an issue altogether climate  change I haven't heard about that  Russian collusion with Trump not  something I'm aware of because I'm  watching Fox News and they're talking  about Hillary and uranium one we are  seeing level three of informational  incongruity on many issues in the United  States right now and it's media like fox  news and info wars and many many others  that are perpetrating that that are  creating that degree of informational  incongruity send me your thoughts about  this really important issue I'm on  Twitter at D Pakman the shows on Twitter  at David Pakman show great to be back in  studio and we have many more stories to  talk about today today's program is made  possible in part by futur futur is a  social forecasting game where you  compete with other players to predict  the future and it's built on the  principles of what's called a prediction  market a scientifically proven way of  using the wisdom of the crowd to create  more accurate predictions about future  events prediction markets have been  shown to work much better than other  forecasting methods like polling or  for analysis in many cases and futur has  actually taken the concept and turned it  into a fun easy to use social game you  open up the futur app and you'll see a  whole range of forecasts covering topics  across the board from politics to sports  and everything in between  you can check out my predictions and  follow me to get updates on my profile  which is linked to in the description if  you're watching this on YouTube the tour  is a great tool to find out more about  the world improve your forecasting  ability show off your prediction skills  to friends and even better when you make  predictions on futur you're helping to  create more accurate forecasts for  everybody their mission of creating  better predictions is great and actually  going in there and seeing how well you  can do at predicting the future can be  kind of addicting go to futur com sign  up and start making forecast it's free  and it's available on both Android and  iOS as well as on web browsers and  that's f you t you you are calm
 

